# Build-context exclusions.
#
# This is the primary control that keeps secrets and runtime state OUT of the
# image. Anything listed here is never sent to the daemon, so it cannot end up
# in a layer even by accident — and layers are forever, `rm` in a later RUN does
# not remove a file from an earlier one.

# --- secrets: never, under any circumstances -------------------------------
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key

# --- runtime state: belongs on the volume, not in a layer -------------------
# Baking a 2.7 GB-and-growing audit database into the image would also make
# every rollback restore a stale hash chain.
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm

# --- host build artefacts: wrong architecture, and they'd shadow the venv ---
.venv/
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
*.egg-info/
src/*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/

# --- not needed at runtime --------------------------------------------------
.git/
.gitignore
.github/
.claude/
tests/
docs/
CLAUDE.md
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
docker-compose.yml
argus.service
argus-shadow.service
argus-shadow.timer
argus-snapshot.service
argus-snapshot.timer
scripts/
.DS_Store
**/.DS_Store

# Writer-lock sidecars — runtime only
*.db.lock
